1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,585
The Curiosity Club.

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:04,971
Episode 14.

3
00:00:04,971 --> 00:00:07,869
The Caterpillar's New Chapter.

4
00:00:07,869 --> 00:00:10,894
Here is something to listen for.

5
00:00:10,894 --> 00:00:15,923
Was the quiet-looking chrysalis a stage with no important changes?

6
00:00:15,923 --> 00:00:17,514
Ready?

7
00:00:17,514 --> 00:00:19,715
Let us find out.

8
00:00:19,715 --> 00:00:24,517
The class follows a butterfly life cycle through a garden camera.

9
00:00:24,517 --> 00:00:28,835
At first, Maya can hardly see the egg on a leaf.

10
00:00:28,835 --> 00:00:32,400
Later, a tiny caterpillar appears.

11
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:35,269
It spends a lot of time eating.

12
00:00:35,269 --> 00:00:37,400
Leo nods.

13
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:40,696
I understand this stage very well.

14
00:00:40,696 --> 00:00:44,715
Over the following days, the caterpillar grows.

15
00:00:44,715 --> 00:00:48,877
The children draw it and write the date beside each picture.

16
00:00:48,877 --> 00:00:51,690
Then it forms a chrysalis.

17
00:00:51,690 --> 00:00:55,099
Now it is doing nothing, says Pip.

18
00:00:55,099 --> 00:01:02,045
We cannot see much movement outside, Ms. Park replies, but important changes are happening inside.

19
00:01:02,045 --> 00:01:05,994
Maya imagines a little workshop adding wings.

20
00:01:05,994 --> 00:01:12,968
Ms. Park explains that the real process is a much bigger change in body form, called metamorphosis.

21
00:01:12,968 --> 00:01:16,349
They keep watching the camera over time.

22
00:01:16,349 --> 00:01:19,971
One day, an adult butterfly emerges.

23
00:01:19,971 --> 00:01:23,593
Its wings are not ready for immediate flight.

24
00:01:23,593 --> 00:01:27,599
They expand, and it rests while they become ready.

25
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:30,369
Leo opens his notebook.

26
00:01:30,369 --> 00:01:37,400
The egg, caterpillar, chrysalis, and butterfly look so different that they could be four different animals.

27
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:41,519
But they are stages in one life cycle, says Maya.

28
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:48,451
Pip draws his own life cycle: small robot, bigger robot, giant robot, school principal.

29
00:01:48,451 --> 00:01:51,946
That is a career plan, Leo tells him.

30
00:01:51,946 --> 00:01:58,281
Pip adds one more stage: giant robot principal who gives everyone extra reading time.

31
00:01:58,281 --> 00:02:02,443
Maya thinks that sounds like a promising new chapter.

32
00:02:02,443 --> 00:02:05,596
Now, a little more to discover.

33
00:02:05,596 --> 00:02:11,065
A butterfly's life cycle includes egg, larva, pupa, and adult.

34
00:02:11,065 --> 00:02:16,377
The caterpillar is the larva, and the chrysalis is the pupal stage.

35
00:02:16,377 --> 00:02:20,468
Metamorphosis changes the insect's body form.

36
00:02:20,468 --> 00:02:25,724
A quiet-looking chrysalis is part of an active biological process.

37
00:02:25,724 --> 00:02:28,892
Let us hear the main idea again.

38
00:02:28,892 --> 00:02:33,323
The class recorded different stages of a butterfly's life.

39
00:02:33,323 --> 00:02:38,082
The chrysalis looked quiet, but major changes were happening.

40
00:02:38,082 --> 00:02:43,806
Keeping dated observations helped the children connect the very different appearances.

41
00:02:43,806 --> 00:02:46,946
Here are three useful expressions.

42
00:02:46,946 --> 00:02:50,127
You can listen, or say them with me.

43
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:52,784
First, we saw an egg.

44
00:02:52,784 --> 00:02:55,440
First, we saw an egg.

45
00:02:55,440 --> 00:02:58,536
Later, it formed a chrysalis.

46
00:02:58,536 --> 00:03:01,633
Later, it formed a chrysalis.

47
00:03:01,633 --> 00:03:03,863
What happened next?

48
00:03:03,863 --> 00:03:06,093
What happened next?

49
00:03:06,093 --> 00:03:09,090
Remember our listening question?

50
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:14,119
Was the quiet-looking chrysalis a stage with no important changes?

51
00:03:14,119 --> 00:03:16,406
Here is the answer.

52
00:03:16,406 --> 00:03:18,068
No.

53
00:03:18,068 --> 00:03:22,713
Major changes were happening inside during the pupal stage.

54
00:03:22,713 --> 00:03:26,676
And here is a question just for your imagination.

55
00:03:26,676 --> 00:03:31,761
What could you observe and draw over several days to notice gradual change?

56
00:03:31,761 --> 00:03:35,071
There is more than one possible answer.

57
00:03:35,071 --> 00:03:38,366
Keep wondering, and see you next time.
